  "term": "Thematic Apperception Test",
  "definition": "Thematic Apperception Test is a projective assessment in which a person is shown selected pictures of social and interpersonal situations and asked to make up a story about each one. The stories are used to explore patterns in interpersonal relationships, reactions to authority and peers, and how inner needs relate to outside demands.",
